<title>ESTONIA: CPI RISES THREE PERCENT IN Q1.</title>
<headline>CPI RISES THREE PERCENT IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian Consumer Price Index rose by three percent in the first quarter, compared to a rise of 1.6 percent in the fourth quarter last year, the statistics office said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Goods inflation was 2.9 percent, including a rise in food products by 1.9 percent and a rise in non-food by 4.6 percent, the office added in a statement.</p>
<p>Inflation in services was 3.1 percent.</p>
<p>Compared to the first quarter of 1996, the prices of goods and services rose by 10.5 percent, the office said.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
